data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":2181,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_01e969450b0b2ccb016acd306921ac87d1a8093ebf5628b161","object":"response","created_at":1791832169,"completed_at":1791832209,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_01e969450b0b2ccb016acd306aa01c87d1b523b1e197e1a9ef","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Exploring project structure**\n\nI'm considering a project that involves creating an array with properties that might seem impossible in JSON, especially under strict typing rules. I’m thinking about how to test this comprehensively while ensuring I maintain enough flexibility. It feels a bit daunting, especially when I want to push the boundaries of what's achievable. I'll need to really focus on not just functionality but also how the positioning and structure can make things work smoothly."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqzTBsS3F8fv9w0l3s88F-hb-ta5pfoROuCaen3fp_mtGEuV81iEH4cvPPdtpdpIXlCBRFAUdTsSn1zILJgTqB5jNJ7urnT19au6BqrEBN2Ut_lwIm4G5YVc4zdfBLMdtBjYj8xi7uHRFqxaeC09ZvyP3rslZHzcB4mVwvkhV7mIpqZENxjfsiaJNFMR4jvOW9MuCb4beEKvu64EhB4MTK-j8q0vTyYoPVBYQ6vkyPt6_3PetBt3YDK9r_YYPrsvuGWYY2kx9yPxrY02vjG_M2jKtFM7LaCMNGrvtcAB8HdsHh0dR33rmzRqT1Vfu3EyQo33m76l-qJIXueBfHHIcljPAqF1W_flbzaxfcmiSClpvr3QduTKi4ORwKSGSvA9V_XYfGMiFRrpgNFiOpk47l0f1On9KN9PbAcL6WQFNL_rmmNPH3CARLO_2UjKKopBNWAuPJOESbLo_BW1reObvi5t8IPIM7WzeQVzdxSKh5gvxSipeB6k0lnHcgjA85TLxjScDCglYgVmuYBK2cpvcz3sJkpDFLdC7wny3_5ua8wiIv3PiYNtS1Nz8ivXS-0oFiA_1G9DAk9bUsSqzgGLcvjWyolP3gqRemYovHBbx-iHinUxAAhRzPbgHKDCyELP2tiR1aTox2sOx482BxY8DwZTb71vdb0zyFZnSUK-3ef0YfFlHuyQ06tv4PaN1qSILsFDWWuarw5S4_PxsPpLZEyENanBWO70RbpPZK1Pn73-GSLm7RSx6bFekHCaTRFe2n3VXFd1hoV5OJhIaXNO5hj-RAsN_RFAIoBspKPmFNw9_MXP3myWafCPVeQb2JJfT4mVk-lJ0ZZAzv6fC8QjhccQa1Q8YOEpLVZdOHbjqTq0KNCwDEwcs1erf4EBfqg0DHEF3oM4yS5v02m2ok3dATL6se0EK6Zz_2EoQ8ocr3iPnZCIMeZebwLaEwJ6td2Aa8WugwCeLjlRsp_w8QKPnCXdIieOdkcDzbeumlOwg_sHU3GXIDTqN_2HwaPmaczLqKsi4YlH-3zCqukLEO8VmpID2BPc_yoFSwj_cm5Ps3fnMYONyTnJFNF7xeTb7W_BE0gEX8_THilxsfaiDeWmyhA1Z4vbZGfDl-07p3ESzS8GQkYt7__DoQuqqfYFoYCDxqL0lfSgHVyZyd65rhmu0umaThNaxMFraquPbUzHdb3kiId4ikiZRDG3_rTpYiWcXE0pDmE8AAygEv44VZZYHmaNapvmbF6isnr5FxZfnzw1XKooFkg2kQHDm6URXe1-UYvzHXPvIpjkCl2ehVlA7IBqiUcdP8JA1YpDYmO72kAhvgdyi-vAkaXv-wzd7O3uSbdEQ3WPyT2-22yjP9azmKUwe43IF7WLqgfRWkPO8vOfTkNYCUxwUm1cK5YQcnZwsYf7dMyPPeNxPbCNFE8k0Z2dqZoyzpQx4L1jGxYYrCDCQep4cKSxu91iHIJEzigVeV5kNHl8GqfXtll2pBG7LlDE5Pcms6YMMWHva5XKw34Zmv7sKjZvJLKCIXyU9IZDJeiFicfRVsq7gjYJGkXfbQlELfzGQu9LXRcHe2gZxCHrRbd4zKH4BaGl2YLbRtIKELxO8Br-S7wBBkqDjHXdSS_y3u6nk2zBImDk13k40Kny4cboXXGoH2JhqU-xW6w820c15TYIjEkG5cXyYKeb5boTsNyTcU9XEWDmMf3gKk7bc7hzBBfDXMMqyXr2II33xF_2IbJ0cJ5WYTRjoGE-v__YkqhO-7R-cffdQ7fPofXzCTkWHTBnp3Bzx6ln0uQLSa0PvMzqUTmKlMrxGZell3ZMw4IY6y0n_3lGKl6mjRW6dFjIjb8NWfGnHr6GOxg16DfTs85ajV2sj37BdgtP4l8kSthO6Rfi4m6eWVa9wltcg9MDY="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_01e969450b0b2ccb016acd306c23fc87d19e331df4e6f264bc","call_id":"call_c817323a41c943678543184533cb2014","name":"write","arguments":"{\"path\":\"test/import.test.js\",\"content\":\"import { test } from 'node:test';\\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { once } from 'node:events';\\nimport { mkdtemp, rm } from 'node:fs/promises';\\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\\nimport { DatabaseSync } from 'node:sqlite';\\n\\ntest('imports validate atomically, preserve portable fields and order, and remain independent across restart', async () => {\\n  const directory = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'workboard-import-'));\\n  const dbPath = join(directory, 'db.sqlite');\\n  let child, base;\\n  async function start() {\\n    child = spawn(process.execPath, ['server.js'], { env: { ...process.env, PORT: '0', DB_PATH: dbPath }, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });\\n    base = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\\n      let output = '';\\n      child.on('error', reject);\\n      child.stdout.on('data', chunk => {\\n        output += chunk;\\n        const match = output.match(/listening on port (\\\\d+)/);\\n        if (match) resolve(`http://127.0.0.1:${match[1]}`);\\n      });\\n    });\\n  }\\n  async function stop() { const exit = once(child, 'exit'); child.kill('SIGTERM'); await exit; child = null; }\\n  const post = (path, body = {}) => fetch(base + path, { method: 'POST', body: new URLSearchParams(body), redirect: 'manual' });\\n  const get = async path => (await fetch(base + path)).text();\\n  const exported = async id => (await fetch(`${base}/projects/${id}/download`)).json();\\n  const snapshot = () => {\\n    const db = new DatabaseSync(dbPath);\\n    try { return ['projects', 'tasks', 'task_positions'].map(table => db.prepare(`SELECT * FROM ${table} ORDER BY rowid`).all()); }\\n    finally { db.close(); }\\n  };\\n  const task = { title: '  First\\\\t TASK  ', completed: true, priority: 'High', dueDate: '0001-01-01', notes: '  \\\\r\\\\n日本語 🌻 <script>literal</script>\\\\rline\\\\n  ', deleted: false };\\n  const document = { format: 'workboard-project', version: 1, project: { name: 'Portable name', archived: true, defaultPriority: 'Low', tasks: [task, { ...task, title: 'Deleted', deleted: true, dueDate: '2000-02-29' }, { ...task, title: 'Last', completed: false, priority: 'Normal', dueDate: '', notes: '' }] } };\\n  try {\\n    await start();\\n    const home = await get('/');\\n    assert.match(home, /<label for=\\\"project-json\\\">Project JSON<\\\\/label>/);\\n    assert.match(home, /<textarea id=\\\"project-json\\\"/);\\n    assert.match(home, />Imported project name<\\\\/label>/);\\n    await post('/projects', { name: 'Original' });\\n    await post('/projects/1/tasks', { title: 'Untouched' });\\n    const before = snapshot();\\n    const invalids = ['{broken', 'null', '[]'];\\n    const mutation = change => { const value = structuredClone(document); change(value); invalids.push(JSON.stringify(value)); };\\n    mutation(value => value.format = 'other');\\n    mutation(value => value.version = '1');\\n    mutation(value => value.version = 2);\\n    mutation(value => delete value.project);\\n    mutation(value => value.project.name = ' \\\\t ');\\n    mutation(value => value.project.archived = 1);\\n    mutation(value => value.project.defaultPriority = 'Urgent');\\n    mutation(value => value.project.tasks = {});\\n    for (const field of Object.keys(task)) mutation(value => delete value.project.tasks[2][field]);\\n    mutation(value => value.project.tasks[2].title = '\\\\n  ');\\n    mutation(value => value.project.tasks[2].completed = 'false');\\n    mutation(value => value.project.tasks[2].priority = 'normal');\\n    mutation(value => value.project.tasks[2].notes = null);\\n    mutation(value => value.project.tasks[2].deleted = 0);\\n    for (const dueDate of ['1900-02-29', '2025-02-29', '0000-01-01', '10000-01-01', '2024-04-31', '2024-1-01', ' 2024-01-01 ', null]) {\\n      mutation(value => value.project.tasks[2].dueDate = dueDate);\\n    }\\n    for (const json of invalids) {\\n      const response = await post('/projects/import', { json, name: '  Retained name  ' });\\n      assert.equal(response.status, 422);\\n      const html = await response.text();\\n      assert.match(html, /role=\\\"alert\\\">Invalid project JSON/);\\n      assert.match(html, /value=\\\"  Retained name  \\\"/);\\n      // JSON source stays in the textarea (HTML escaping is intentional).\\n      assert.ok(html.includes(json.replace(/[&<>\\\"']/g, character => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '\\\"': '&quot;', \\\"'\\\": '&#39;' }[character]))));\\n      assert.deepEqual(snapshot(), before);\\n    }\\n    const blank = await post('/projects/import', { json: JSON.stringify(document), name: ' \\\\t ' });\\n    assert.match(await blank.text(), /role=\\\"alert\\\">Project name is required/);\\n    assert.deepEqual(snapshot(), before);\\n    // Extra properties cannot set identities or remembered positions.\\n    document.project.id = 1;\\n    document.project.tasks[0].id = 1;\\n    document.project.tasks[0].position = 999;\\n    const response = await post('/projects/import', { json: JSON.stringify(document), name: '  Imported  copy  ' });\\n    assert.equal(response.status, 303);\\n    assert.equal(response.headers.get('location'), '/projects/2');\\n    const expected = { ...document.project, name: 'Imported  copy', tasks: document.project.tasks.map(({ id, position, ...value }) => ({ ...value, notes: value.notes.replace(/\\\\r\\\\n?/g, '\\\\n') })) };\\n    delete expected.id;\\n    assert.deepEqual((await exported(2)).project, expected);\\n    assert.deepEqual(snapshot().map(rows => rows.filter(row => row.id === 1 || row.task_id === 1)), before);\\n    const archived = await get('/projects/2?filter=Deleted');\\n    assert.match(archived, /Archived project/);\\n    assert.match(archived, /disabled>Restore task/);\\n    assert.match(archived, /<textarea[^>]*disabled/);\\n    await post('/projects/2/restore');\\n    assert.match(await get('/'), /2\\\\/2 completed|1\\\\/2 completed/);\\n    const restored = await post('/projects/2/tasks/3/restore', { filter: 'Deleted' });\\n    assert.match(restored.headers.get('location'), /filter=Deleted/);\\n    assert.deepEqual((await exported(2)).project.tasks.map(value => value.title), ['  First\\\\t TASK  ', 'Deleted', 'Last']);\\n    await post('/projects/2/tasks/2/move', { destination: '1' });\\n    await post('/projects/2/tasks', { title: 'New' });\\n    await post('/projects/1/tasks/2/rename', { title: 'Changed after move' });\\n    await post('/projects/1/tasks/2/move', { destination: '2' });\\n    assert.deepEqual((await exported(2)).project.tasks.map(value => value.title), ['Changed after move', 'Deleted', 'Last', 'New']);\\n    assert.equal((await exported(2)).project.tasks[0].priority, 'High');\\n    assert.equal((await exported(2)).project.tasks[3].priority, 'Low');\\n    assert.equal((await exported(1)).project.tasks[0].title, 'Untouched');\\n    const empty = structuredClone(document);\\n    empty.project.tasks = [];\\n    const emptyResponse = await post('/projects/import', { json: JSON.stringify(empty), name: 'Empty' });\\n    assert.equal(emptyResponse.headers.get('location'), '/projects/3');\\n    assert.deepEqual((await exported(3)).project.tasks, []);\\n    const saved = snapshot();\\n    await stop(); await start();\\n    assert.deepEqual(snapshot(), saved);\\n    assert.equal((await exported(2)).project.tasks[0].notes, task.notes.replace(/\\\\r\\\\n?/g, '\\\\n'));\\n    assert.equal((await exported(3)).project.archived, true);\\n  } finally {\\n    if (child) await stop();\\n    await rm(directory, { recursive: true, force: true });\\n  }\\n});\\n\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","offset","limit"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},{"type":"null"}]},"limit":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":true},{"type":"function","name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command","timeout"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":true},{"type":"function","name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[]